<no>2</no><heading guid="_3e63b79f-c3db-49c0-aaef-b6ea0edb88a6"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5214e92a-8470-424b-aefc-c0d1e4508421"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Sections 1 and 2 shall commence on the date of
assent to this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_01f9815d-b854-4b52-973c-a4dc4efd22b7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except as provided by subsection (1), this Act
shall commence on such day as may be appointed by the Governor and notified by
proclamation published in the Gazette.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_874a4b85-e041-4cd6-bea1-bf53a34a4be6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_1c48f454-24a2-4c2a-9cc4-1f7348dd0753"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Reference of certain matters relating to
children</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3cc8cbd7-02c7-4b43-9955-f02c2733ab04"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following matters, to the extent to which
they are not otherwise included in the legislative powers of the Parliament of
the Commonwealth, are referred to the Parliament of the Commonwealth for a
period commencing on the day on which this Act commences and ending on the day
fixed, pursuant to section 4, as the day on which the reference under this
section shall terminate, but no longer, namely&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_5492df11-b36d-4ec9-984e-ee115120ff96" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the maintenance of children and the payment of
expenses in relation to children or child bearing,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6d84022f-de85-44c7-9698-8dfc50dcba2d" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the custody and guardianship of, and access to,
children,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9112fbe7-b964-4f43-a6e2-0c23d3765e08" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the determination of a child&#8217;s parentage
for the purposes of the law of the Commonwealth, whether or not the
determination of the child&#8217;s parentage is incidental to the
determination of any other matter within the legislative powers of the
Commonwealth.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ee281181-1c9e-4e8e-9728-9c26ba70cb97"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to subsection (2A), the matters referred
by subsection (1) do not include the matter of the adoption of children or the
matter of the taking, or the making of provision for or in relation to
authorising the taking, of action that would prevent or interfere
with&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_49977b0a-1c34-43ad-a411-d6288f4b22c8" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a Minister of the Crown, an officer of the State,
an officer of an adoption agency approved under a law of the State, or any
other person or body, having or acquiring the custody, guardianship, care or
control of children under a provision specified in Schedule
1,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4bb2f39d-54b0-48bb-96fe-0651687bb3a4" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.b"
status="repealed">
<no>(b)</no>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e9cb4faa-d986-480a-a552-150e9affd7fd" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court to make
orders in respect of children who are in such custody, guardianship, care or
control, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3ee8eb64-65c0-464b-a54e-b562b38d5e2c" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the jurisdiction of a court of the State, or
other body, under a provision specified in Schedule 1, to make orders, or take
any other action, in respect of&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_76b07e35-85b5-4702-9abe-92c54bf03035"
id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.d-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the custody, guardianship, care or control of
children, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_64d23d85-d49b-4615-bb45-f3431335005f"
id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.d-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">access to children or the supervision of
children.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2A">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a278c897-a423-402f-a8c0-42165e06cd0f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2A"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2A)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The matters referred by subsection (1) include
the matter of the taking, or the making of provision for or in relation to
authorising the taking, of action that would prevent or interfere with a
matter referred to in subsection (2)(a)&#8211;(d) if&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1044faf8-dfb3-44c1-a7d2-243ff9b07aed" id="sec.3-ssec.2A-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Minister of the Crown responsible for the
administration of the relevant provision specified in Schedule 1,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d46dddfd-2bc6-425c-a922-1e8b11718b66" id="sec.3-ssec.2A-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a person authorised, in writing, by that Minister
of the Crown to act on his or her behalf for the purposes of Part VII of the
<legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Family
Law Act 1975</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth, as amended and in force
for the time being,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">consents, in writing, to the taking of such action by
way of instituting, or continuing, proceedings under that Act in a court
having jurisdiction under that Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6f8bb46a-e89e-4232-ad3a-d15be6cbceba"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In the preceding provisions of this
section&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b9d259e0-65ce-469c-ab17-10095b6904b6" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the references to children shall be read as
references to persons under the age of 18 years,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0d9c8753-03e9-41b2-acc7-436692cb7b3f" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the references to the maintenance of, and the
payment of expenses in relation to, children shall be read as including
references to the maintenance of, and the payment of expenses in relation to,
persons who have attained that age and have special needs in respect of
maintenance or expenses by reason of being engaged in a course of education or
training or by reason of a physical or mental handicap,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_95d211d1-2017-4997-b6a8-28df22f683ff" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the references to a provision specified in
Schedule 1 shall be read as references to the provision as amended and in
force from time to time, and as including a reference to any provision or
provisions replacing that provision and as amended and in force from time to
time.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 1989 No 132,
Sch 1; 1996 No 60, Sch 1 (1)&#8211;(6).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4ce5e166-4634-4aec-bed8-55265777a4af"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_c552e6e8-ee00-44d1-b1cc-13793be9d6f9"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Termination of reference</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, at any time, by proclamation
published on the NSW legislation website, fix a day as the day on which the
reference under this Act shall terminate.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Am 2009 No 106,
Sch 3.10.</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


